+{"sections":[{"topic":"authority","conclusion":"The authority system uses fresh AgentDirectory snapshots for every decision, ensuring no caching of stale authorization states. Permissions are enforced through strict descendant ownership checks using AgentOwnershipGraph, preventing cross-subtree operations. The system separates durable identity from live Supervisor state, allowing future control plane implementations without inheriting internal details.","evidence":[{"path":"src/traceh/supervision/authority.py","start_line":3,"end_line":8},{"path":"src/traceh/supervision/authority.py","start_line":100,"end_line":109}]},{"topic":"budget","conclusion":"Subtasks reserve budget through the BudgetLedgerService.reserve_child method which creates immutable budget facts. The main agent retains closing budget by maintaining separate budget accounts and using idempotent operations that prevent double-charging. Budget reservations are append-only facts that are projected rather than stored as mutable balances.","evidence":[{"path":"src/traceh/budgets/service.py","start_line":118,"end_line":120},{"path":"src/traceh/budgets/projection.py","start_line":1,"end_line":7}]},{"topic":"lifecycle","conclusion":"The lifecycle system ensures no running work remains through admission leases, disposal scopes, and final close blocking. Creation/cancellation uses ownership lineage projection from AgentDirectory, while cleanup waits for all admitted work to complete. Products are captured through the event store mechanism which records immutable facts about budget usage and reservations.","evidence":[{"path":"src/traceh/supervision/lifecycle.py","start_line":1,"end_line":15},{"path":"src/traceh/supervision/lifecycle.py","start_line":43,"end_line":80}]}]}
